{#
  The `PUID`/`PGID`/`TZ` env entries every linuxserver.io (LSIO) container takes. An LSIO image
  starts as root, chowns its config tree to `PUID:PGID` and drops to that uid, so the three
  keys travel together and a copy that loses one is a container that runs as the image's
  default `abc` uid 911 or logs in UTC.

  Use it only for an LSIO image. A literal `runAsUser: 1000` elsewhere in the fleet is the uid
  an image bakes in (n8n's `node`, karakeep's built tagger, cloudflare-ddns), which equals
  `puid` by coincidence; tying it to `puid` would move it when the operator's uid moves. A
  non-LSIO container that wants only `TZ` writes the two-line entry out (#3729 measured that
  a one-line call saves nothing there).

  Indentation is fixed at 12 spaces, the `env:` list depth of a container in a Deployment pod
  template. The call goes on its own line straight after `env:`; other entries follow it.
  The `lsio-env-is-the-macro` row of ansible/tests/repo/test_census_rows_roles.py holds every
  `PUID` and `PGID` entry to this macro.
#}
{% macro lsio_env() %}
            - name: PUID
              value: "{{ puid }}"
            - name: PGID
              value: "{{ pgid }}"
            - name: TZ
              value: "{{ tz }}"
{%- endmacro %}
